  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n- X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧おごる (to treat someone to X)\n- おごって⟦もらう→もらう：00520_morau⟧ (to be treated by someone)\n- おごって⟦あげる→あげる：00546_ageru⟧ (to treat someone - giving perspective)\n- おごって⟦くれる→くれる：00724_kureru⟧ (to treat someone - receiving perspective)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{割|わ}り{勘|かん}→割り勘：08156_warikan⟧ (splitting the bill - opposite concept)\n- ⟦ご{馳走|ちそう}→ご馳走：01336_gochisou⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to treat - more formal)\n- ⟦{払|はら}って→払う：00535_harau⟧⟦あげる→あげる：00546_ageru⟧ (to pay for someone)\n\nINFORMAL KANJI:\nSometimes written as {奢|おご}る, but hiragana is more common.\n\nUSAGE:\nDifferent from {驕|おご}る (to be arrogant), which is a separate word with a different meaning.",
